    "topic": "The rough-nuisance Wasserstein frontier for marginal counterfactual generation. Fix integers d>=1 and m>=3, smoothness alpha,beta,s>0, radius L>=10. Observe n iid (X,A,Y), X uniform on [0,1]^d with this design law known, A binary, Y in [0,1]^m. Consistency and ignorability Y(a) independent of A given X hold. The unknown propensity e(x)=P(A=1|X=x) belongs to H_d^alpha(L) and lies in [1/4,3/4]. The conditional density eta(y|x) of Y given A=1,X=x integrates to 1 in y for every x and satisfies 1/2<=eta<=3/2. For every y its x-section lies in H_d^beta(L); for every x its y-section lies in H_m^s(L); no mixed derivative condition is imposed. The A=0 conditional density is fixed uniform, carrying no additional restrictions linking arm1 to arm0. H_k^t(L) uses r=ceil(t)-1: all partial derivatives through order r bounded by L, and order-r partial derivatives Holder of exponent t-r with constant L (integer t means Lipschitz derivatives of order t-1). The target probability law Q1 has density q1(y)=integral eta(y|x) dx, the law of Y(1). Risk is inf over all measurable probability-valued estimators Qhat of sup over this class E[W1(Qhat,Q1)], with Euclidean transport cost. Constants may depend on d,m,alpha,beta,s,L, never n. Each fixed parameter tuple has asymptotic n scope; no adaptation to unknown smoothness is required. KERNEL: Determine, up to positive constants including every unavoidable critical logarithmic factor, the minimax W1 risk R_n(d,m,alpha,beta,s) on the specified class; construct one explicit finite-data probability-valued estimator attaining it and a matching same-class all-estimator converse. Derive the necessary-and-sufficient smoothness/dimension boundary for R_n having the oracle order n^{-(s+1)/(2s+m)} and derive the sharp rate in every non-oracle region. The exact formula and whether candidate interaction regimes exist are answer-open; a guessed phase diagram is not imposed. The hard theorem is the full matching frontier, with a nonempty non-oracle region derived or, if none exists, a uniform constructive oracle-attainment theorem that explains why rough nuisance does not impose a cost on this whole class. The latter alternative must independently survive the prior-art and flagship gate; no scalar lower bound or oracle-only upper theorem counts as completion. Estimator algebra, projection orders, least-favorable mixtures and proof mechanics are delegated. Explicitly position which subfamilies embed into the published DoubleGen target model; do not claim class containment of its full nuisance framework. COMPUTATION: Construct empirical multiresolution outcome coefficients with finite-order propensity/outcome bias corrections in a known-design covariate basis, then a finite-dimensional minimum-distance projection onto nonnegative unit-mass measures on a refining outcome grid. The output is a discrete probability measure with an executable categorical sampler. Select the finite resolutions and correction order by the known class inputs. This is a proposed concrete algorithm family, not an assumption that its unproved error certificate holds; the solver may derive another explicit algorithm if necessary. CONSUMER: The public DoubleGen implementation and its counterfactual image-generation experiment (Luedtke–Fukumizu 2025, arXiv2509.16842, Section 6.1 and Appendix M.1) and Dance–Xi–Orbanz–Bloem-Reddy DecFM (arXiv2605.07665) generate precisely marginal counterfactual outcome distributions from confounded observations. The frontier tells these methods when increasing generator capacity cannot compensate for rough nuisance learning and supplies a positive reconstruction benchmark/correction alternative. The theorem is for a smooth compact positive-density model and is a theoretical calibration of continuous-output generation, not a claim that raw CelebA pixels satisfy every Holder assumption. npcausal and the published HIV CD4 density application in Kennedy et al Biometrika2023 are additional distributional consumers; the scalar case is not claimed covered by m>=3. PRIOR-ART CONSTRAINT: DoubleGen Section 7 explicitly leaves rough-nuisance optimality open, but Kennedy ACIC 2023 already announces counterfactual-density minimax rates. Establish a substantive new marginal W1 theorem; do not claim first counterfactual-density minimax theory, substitute averaged conditional Wasserstein loss, or present an unmatched bracket as completion.\n\nPRESOLVE EVIDENCE REQUIRING VERIFICATION: The draft constructs smooth, positive, normalized conditional densities with one propensity sign per covariate cell shared across outcome cells. Mixing these signs leaves a deterministic marginal product perturbation. Its displayed all-count mixture calculation gives a proposed Hellinger bound proportional to n^2 h^d delta^m b^2(a^2+b^2), where a scales as h^alpha and b as min(h^beta,delta^s). For d=1,m=6,s=4,alpha=beta=27/200, the resulting Wasserstein lower exponent 243/697 is strictly smaller than the scalar comparator 27/77 and oracle exponent 5/14. Exact exponent arithmetic and a finite normalization/leakage diagnostic were independently checked; the continuous proof remains unverified. An exact weighted Galerkin identity supplies a scale-dependent bias reduction, and finite Kantorovich–Rubinstein projection supplies a probability reconstruction route.\nUNRESOLVED BOTTLENECK: Prove the high-rank higher-order coefficient variance certificate, then match the full asymmetric frontier and critical logarithms. The ACIC2023 density announcement remains a priority-comparison obligation. The isolated lower bound is not completion.\nEARLY KILL TEST: Independently audit the balanced interaction family and full-sample bound, then test a concrete truncated correction at that tuple. Stop the novelty claim if exact prior art subsumes it; do not infer impossibility from failure of one naive correction.\nSTRONGEST-FORM DRAFT (unverified, gaps listed inside): <repo-root>/internal/presolve_drafts/stat_counterfact